// Lesson 7.3 — Ladders I: Climbing with isPlatformer
// Level 3 (Outline Only, Short Lesson ~15 min): reuse PlayerController.Update()'s
// existing `if (!isPlatformer)` 2D movement branch!
// Entering a "Ladder" trigger sets `isPlatformer = false;` (and `rb.gravityScale = 0;`);
// exiting sets `isPlatformer = true;` (and `rb.gravityScale = gravityScale;`).
// Remaining class time goes to Cave Level Studio & getting ready for the boss fight.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
import { renderAskBanner } from '../../lib/walkthrough';
import { renderDecompose } from '../../lib/decompose';

const DECOMPOSE = {
  big: 'Let the player climb ladders up and down without writing a second movement controller.',
  parts: [
    {
      name: 'Mark every ladder object with a Ladder trigger collider',
      doc: '2.1 (creating and assigning tags, plus Collider2D Is Trigger)',
      href: '2.1.html',
    },
    {
      name: 'Switch out of platformer mode on trigger enter',
      doc: '`PlayerController.OnTriggerEnter2D()` (`CompareTag("Ladder")` -> `isPlatformer = false;` and `rb.gravityScale = 0;`)',
      href: '6.1.html',
    },
    {
      name: 'Restore platformer mode on trigger exit',
      doc: '`PlayerController.OnTriggerExit2D()` (`CompareTag("Ladder")` -> `isPlatformer = true;` and `rb.gravityScale = gravityScale;`)',
      href: '4.4.html',
    },
  ],
  why:
    'Look at `PlayerController.Update()`: you ALREADY wrote `if (!isPlatformer) { rb.linearVelocity = new Vector2(xVector, yVector); }`. When you touch a ladder, you already have a mode switch that turns vertical `W`/`S` input on — all a ladder needs is flipping `isPlatformer` and zeroing gravity while overlapping the trigger.',
  turns: [
    'Look at `PlayerController.Update()`: why does setting `isPlatformer = false;` make vertical climbing (`W`/`S` or Up/Down arrows) work immediately without writing any new `rb.linearVelocity` line?',
    'In addition to setting `isPlatformer = false;`, why is it helpful to set `rb.gravityScale = 0;` on trigger enter and restore `rb.gravityScale = gravityScale;` on exit?',
    'If your ladder is solid instead of marked `Is Trigger`, which callback fires instead — and why would the player fail to walk onto the ladder?',
  ],
};

const body = `
${renderAskBanner('how do I climb a ladder?', 3)}

<p class="lead">
    <strong>Short lesson (~15 min) + Cave Level Studio.</strong> Your
    <code>PlayerController.Update()</code> already switches between top-down movement
    (<code>if (!isPlatformer)</code>) and gravity-driven platforming (<code>else</code>).
    Today you reuse that single boolean: touching a <code>"Ladder"</code> trigger sets
    <code>isPlatformer = false</code>, and leaving sets <code>isPlatformer = true</code>.
    Then spend the rest of class building out your cave level for the boss fight.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
${renderDecompose('7.3', DECOMPOSE, 3)}

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Editor: Set Up the Ladder Trigger (~5 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~5 min</span>
    </div>

    <ol>
        <li>Open <code>Assets/Scenes/Platformer.unity</code> and select Tag Manager (Inspector → Tag → <strong>Add Tag...</strong>) to add a tag named <code>Ladder</code> (exact spelling).</li>
        <li>Place your ladder sprite/GameObject in the cave, tag it <code>Ladder</code>, attach a <code>BoxCollider2D</code>, and check <strong>Is Trigger</strong>.</li>
        <li>Adjust Sorting Layer / Order in Layer so the player draws <em>in front of</em> the ladder rungs while climbing.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Code: Toggle isPlatformer in Trigger Callbacks (~10 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~10 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Open <code>Assets/Scripts/PlayerController.cs</code>. You already have
        <code>OnTriggerEnter2D(Collider2D other)</code> and <code>OnTriggerExit2D(Collider2D other)</code>:
    </p>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Callback</th><th>Condition</th><th>What to set inside the branch</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>OnTriggerEnter2D(Collider2D other)</code></td>
            <td><code>other.gameObject.CompareTag("Ladder")</code></td>
            <td><code>isPlatformer = false;</code> and <code>rb.gravityScale = 0;</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>OnTriggerExit2D(Collider2D other)</code></td>
            <td><code>other.gameObject.CompareTag("Ladder")</code></td>
            <td><code>isPlatformer = true;</code> and <code>rb.gravityScale = gravityScale;</code></td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="callout">
        <strong>Why zero <code>rb.gravityScale</code> only for ladders?</strong> Notice we stored
        <code>[SerializeField] float gravityScale;</code> in <a href="6.1.html">6.1</a> instead of
        hardcoding a constant. When exiting a ladder trigger, setting
        <code>rb.gravityScale = gravityScale;</code> returns the exact weight you tuned in the Inspector.
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Reusing State</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>In <code>PlayerController.Update()</code>, pressing <code>KeyCode.J</code> only fires inside the <code>else</code> branch of <code>if (!isPlatformer)</code>. Does jumping work while climbing, and is that what your cave wants?</li>
            <li>What happens if you climb past the top of the ladder trigger box while still holding Up — which callback runs the frame your collider leaves the trigger?</li>
            <li>Why does checking <code>other.gameObject.CompareTag("Ladder")</code> keep coins, enemy swings, and fireballs from accidentally putting the player into climbing mode?</li>
            <li>What would break if you hardcoded <code>rb.gravityScale = 1;</code> on exit when your <code>Player</code> prefab expects <code>gravityScale = 4.5</code>?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Studio Time: Build Out Your Cave Level (~50 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~50 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        With ladders working, spend the rest of class shaping <code>Platformer.unity</code> toward the upcoming boss fight:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Connect lower and upper shafts using a mix of <strong>ladders</strong>, <strong>moving platforms</strong> (<a href="6.3.html">6.3</a>), and tagged <code>Ground</code> jumps.</li>
        <li>Place <code>TurretController</code> hazards and patrolling <code>EnemyController</code> enemies to guard shortcuts or coins.</li>
        <li>Test the entire cave from <code>Start (index 0)</code> → <code>Overworld</code> → <code>Platformer</code> so every room flows toward where your boss door will sit.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="checklist">
    <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Enter a <code>"Ladder"</code> trigger and climb up/down smoothly using <code>isPlatformer = false</code></li>
        <li>Exit the ladder trigger back into normal gravity and platforming (<code>isPlatformer = true</code>)</li>
        <li>Build out multi-level shafts in your cave combining ladders, moving platforms, and enemies</li>
        <li>Commit and push</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-07/index.html">Unit 7: Level Building &amp; Ladders</a> — ladder state &amp; level layout notes</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/triggers-vs-collisions.html">Triggers vs Collisions</a> — <code>OnTriggerEnter2D()</code> and <code>OnTriggerExit2D()</code></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/ask.html">How do I&hellip;? index</a> — find this lesson again by the question you were asking</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="7.4.html">7.4 — Ladders II: Collider Fit &amp; Cave Level Studio</a> — polish ladder tops/bottoms and keep building the cave.</p>
</div>`;
